   "challenges": [
    "Alert volume swung again: 2 445 to 1 705 to 2 610 across three cuts (-30.3% then +53.1%). SR109 asked for the completeness and time window of the reporting to be checked; SR110 and SR111 both publish no correction, so this is now three violent swings in four cuts and the series should be treated as unreadable for transmission signal, not just noisy.",
    "PoE/PoC report completeness is 82.8% (96/116), weakest at Haut-Uele (64.0%) and Sud-Kivu (55.5%). Only 1 of 11 strategic Ituri points runs uninterrupted: Avakubi is closed for security and eight further Ituri PoC (Nzebi, Frigo, Galay, Pont Ituri, Makoko 2, Mabakese, Bey, Foner Mambasa) are on strike over unpaid wages.",
    "Contact follow-up fell to 86.5% from 89.0% the cut before, weakest in Tshopo at 59.8% (211/353); Wamba health zone in Tshopo did not report its contact data this edition.",
    "Care capacity: Nord-Kivu CTE/CT is oversaturated at 118.6% (261 patients, 220 beds); the Nizi CTE in Ituri is saturated for suspects.",
    "Sud-Kivu and Bas-Uele both publish no isolation block this edition, unlike SR110 which had five of six provinces reporting. The four published blocks (758) fall 12 short of the printed national 770; that gap is preserved rather than distributed across the silent provinces."
